ns is nontrivial; we use strict templating and human/LLM verification. The parametric-knowledge signal may be inseparable from a generic difficulty/uncertainty signal, weakening the tug-of-war framing; the separability analysis, step-wise trajectory (persistence, not just magnitude), and causal steering address this. Steering could push activations off-distribution and degrade coherence; matched-random-direction controls and sample-validity checks are included, and suppression might hurt cases where real-world knowledge is legitimately needed (specificity check on belief-consistent items). Effects may be small in strongly instruction-tuned models trained to follow hypotheticals (a valuable boundary condition) and may be model-family and scale specific. Reasoning-length measurement requires clear think/answer delimiters; truncate-and-resume is compute-heavy, so we subsample.'}

