Action: FinalizeIdea
Arguments: {"idea": {"Name": "notation_mode_economy", "Title": "Thinking in Prose When Symbols Would Do: A Notation-Mode Representation That Sets a Surface-Form Compute Tax in Reasoning Models", "Short Hypothesis": "Reasoning models default to a verbose natural-language 'narration mode' for computations that could be expressed in a far terser symbolic/equational mode carrying the identical logical content, incurring a surface-notation compute tax independent of the problem's genuine reasoning depth. Which mode the model uses is set by a linearly-decodable notation-mode representation at the prompt boundary, before any reasoning token is emitted, and steering it toward the symbolic mode cuts tokens with minimal accuracy loss on symbol-amenable problems.", "Related Work": "Two literatures meet but never connect. (1) Notation/paradigm-choice work shows that natural-language vs symbolic reasoning changes ACCURACY and proposes external meta-selectors to pick a paradigm per problem (HybridMind 2024; Chain-of-Reasoning/CoR 2025; H-STAR 2024; Adaptive LLM-Symbolic Reasoning 2025; LLMs are In-Context Semantic rather than Symbolic Reasoners 2023). (2) CoT-compressibility work shows non-result 'glue' tokens are largely removable and that CoT tokens act like program variables (Chain-of-Thought Tokens are Computer Program Variables 2025; KisMATH 2025), and efficiency-steering work shows verbose vs concise paths are linearly separable and steerable (Efficiency Steering 2025; When More is Less 2025). Crucially, NO prior work (a) frames the model's SPONTANEOUS choice of surface notation as an inference-time COMPUTE tax measured on matched problems, (b) shows the model defaults to verbose narration even when a terse symbolic derivation carries the identical computation, (c) dissociates notation-mode from genuine reasoning depth, or (d) locates and causally steers a pre-generation notation-mode representation that sets it. Paradigm-selection work uses external selectors and targets accuracy, not internal cause or compute; compressibility work shows tokens CAN be removed post-hoc but does not identify a controllable internal mode. This is distinct from all my prior proposals (which concern answer-commitment, verification, length priors, framing, scheduling, dimensional units), which never touch surface-notation economy.", "Abstract": "Reasoning language models produce long chains of thought, and it is assumed their length reflects how much reasoning a problem requires. We identify a different, largely orthogonal source of waste: the SURFACE NOTATION the model chooses to think in. The same computation can be written as verbose natural-language narration ('First, we take the total number of apples, which is forty-two, and then we subtract the twelve that were given away...') or as a terse symbolic derivation ('42 - 12 = 30'), and we hypothesize that reasoning models default to the verbose narration mode even when the symbolic mode would carry identical logical content in a fraction of the tokens, incurring a notation compute tax independent of genuine reasoning depth. We further hypothesize that which mode is used is set before generation by a linearly-decodable notation-mode representation at the prompt boundary. Across GSM8K, MATH500, AIME, and GPQA on open reasoning models (DeepSeek-R1 distills 1.5B-14B, Qwen3), we (1) quantify per-problem notation verbosity (narration-to-symbol token ratio) and estimate the token savings of an equivalent symbolic rendering via matched terse re-derivations; (2) show the tax is dissociable from reasoning depth via a mixed-effects decomposition and truncate-and-resume minimal-solve length; (3) train linear probes on prompt-boundary activations to decode the notation mode and test separability from a difficulty probe; (4) causally validate via activation patching (patch a symbolic-mode state into a narration context and observe a mode switch); and (5) deploy a training-free notation-mode steer that induces symbolic reasoning on symbol-amenable problems, measuring tokens-at-equal-accuracy versus verbosity steering and terseness prompting. Our work reframes a slice of overthinking as a surface-notation choice with an identifiable, steerable internal cause, and maps the boundary where symbolic terseness starts to cost accuracy.", "Experiments": "1) Quantify the notation tax (behavioral): Segment CoT into steps. For each step, classify its notation as narration (natural-language prose describing a computation), symbolic/equational (equations, inequalities, compact derivations), or mixed, via parsing (regex for operators/equations) plus LLM-judge; compute a per-trace narration-to-symbol token ratio and a symbol-amenability label per problem (does the solution reduce to a chain of equations/derivations?). For symbol-amenable problems, produce a matched terse SYMBOLIC re-rendering of the SAME solution (prompt the model to rewrite its own correct solution as a compact symbolic derivation, verified to reach the same answer and same steps by LLM-judge) and measure the token savings = narration tokens minus symbolic tokens. Report the distribution of the notation tax across datasets and model sizes. Establish that models default to narration even on highly symbol-amenable problems.\n2) Dissociation from reasoning depth: Fit a mixed-effects model of reasoning-token count with random effect for problem identity (intrinsic difficulty / genuine step count) and a fixed effect for realized notation mode; test whether notation mode explains token count beyond problem identity. Use truncate-and-resume to estimate minimal-solve step count (genuine reasoning depth) and show the notation tax is the tokens-per-step overhead, not extra steps. Compare narration-heavy vs symbol-heavy traces on the SAME problems (across sampled generations) for token count at equal accuracy.\n3) Notation-mode probing (Location): At the prompt boundary (last prompt token, before any reasoning token), extract residual-stream activations and train a linear probe to predict the notation mode the trace will use (narration-dominant vs symbolic-dominant), and separately to predict the realized narration-to-symbol ratio. Metrics: AUROC / R^2, layer sweep. Test separability from a difficulty probe (trained on pass-rate) and a length probe via principal angles between the notation-mode direction and the difficulty/length directions and via joint-model predictive gain. Key claim: notation mode is decodable pre-generation and is not merely a proxy for difficulty or total length.\n4) Causal validation (Causal Intervention): Use activation patching to locate components carrying the notation-mode signal; patch a symbolic-mode prompt-boundary state (from a symbol-amenable, symbolically-solved context) into a narration-mode context for the same problem and test whether the model switches to symbolic reasoning (narration-to-symbol ratio drops, token count drops, answer preserved). Controls: matched-random-direction patch; off-target accuracy preserved; report sign, dose-response, specificity. Reverse patch (symbolic -> narration) to confirm bidirectionality.\n5) Notation-mode steer (training-free intervention): Derive a notation-mode steering direction (difference-of-means between symbolic-dominant and narration-dominant prompt-boundary states). When the probe predicts a problem is symbol-amenable, steer at problem onset toward the symbolic mode. Evaluate on GSM8K, MATH500, AIME, GPQA. Baselines: no intervention, single verbosity/length steering (Efficiency Steering / ASC-style), terseness prompting ('use compact symbolic notation'), external paradigm-selection prompting (HybridMind-style), fixed truncation. Metrics: accuracy (overall and per difficulty stratum), mean tokens, tokens-at-equal-accuracy, narration-to-symbol ratio shift, wall-clock speedup. Key comparison: does targeted notation-mode steering Pareto-dominate blunt verbosity steering, because it removes narration overhead while preserving the computation?\n6) Boundary/failure analysis: Map where symbolic terseness starts to HURT accuracy (e.g., hard AIME/GPQA problems where narration scaffolds intermediate reasoning, or non-symbol-amenable problems). Measure accuracy drop vs steering strength and symbol-amenability, identifying a safe operating regime and testing whether narration is load-bearing on hard problems (an informative boundary condition).\n7) Generalization: transfer probe and steering direction across datasets and model scales without retraining; test whether larger/more-capable models already default to more symbolic (terser) notation (a notation analog of the simplicity bias in When More is Less).", "Experiments_note": "", "Risk Factors and Limitations": "Classifying notation mode (narration vs symbolic vs mixed) is noisy; we mitigate with parsing plus LLM-judge and human spot-checks, reporting agreement. Producing a matched terse symbolic rendering that provably carries the IDENTICAL computation is nontrivial and could drop genuinely necessary reasoning; we verify same-answer and same-step-structure via LLM-judge and human validation, and treat cases where symbolic rendering changes the reasoning as excluded. The notation-mode signal may be inseparable from a difficulty or length signal (harder problems may genuinely warrant narration), which would collapse the phenomenon into existing verbosity work; the separability analysis, mixed-effects dissociation, and causal patching directly test this, and a null separability result is itself an informative finding. Narration may be load-bearing on hard problems (it scaffolds intermediate state), so steering toward symbolic terseness could cause underthinking; the boundary analysis and per-stratum accuracy quantify this trade-off and may show the intervention only helps symbol-amenable, easy-to-medium problems. Steering/patching can push activations off-distribution and confound accuracy reads; matched-random-direction controls and sample-validity checks are included. Intervention gains may not exceed strong verbosity-steering baselines on tokens alone, but the mechanistic reframing (a surface-notation compute tax with a decodable, steerable pre-generation mode representation) is a standalone contribution. Reasoning-length/notation measurement requires clear think/answer delimiters; truncate-and-resume and matched re-rendering are compute-heavy, so we subsample. Effects may be model-family and scale specific."}}
